DTSTAMP:20261111T200147Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54003649862388-54003649862389@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Reception: Stanford Archaeology Center (500-106). Appetizers a
 nd drinks provided from 5:00 p.m. to 5:30 p.m.\n\nTalk description:  The r
 ecent discovery of a Buddha statue in Berenike---the first West of Afghani
 stan---confirms the presence of Buddhists in Hellenistic Egypt. This talk 
 argues that the Therapeutae\, a monastic community of men and women descri
 bed by Philo of Alexandria in On the Contemplative Life---long thought to 
 be Jewish---were actually Buddhist.\n\nShort bio: M. D. Usher is the Lyma
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://classics.stanford.edu/events/all-upcom
 ing-events\nLast synced: 2026-11-11 12:01 PST
